 to numbers so corr() can be used\ntarget_corr = data_clean.astype(float).corr()[\"target\"].sort_values(ascending=False)\n\ndisplay(target_corr.round(3))\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\ntarget_corr.drop(\"target\").plot(kind=\"barh\")\nplt.title(\"Correlation of Each Feature with Heart Disease\")\nplt.xlabel(\"Correlation with Target\")\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-15T09:39:36.171138Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-15T09:39:36.171508Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-15T09:39:36.32852Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-15T09:39:36.171476Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-15T09:39:36.327781Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"target      1.000\ncp          0.432\nthalach     0.420\nslope       0.344\nrestecg     0.135\nfbs        -0.027\nchol       -0.081\ntrestbps   -0.146\nage        -0.221\nsex        -0.284\nthal       -0.362\noldpeak    -0.429\nexang      -0.436\nca         -0.464\nName: target, dtype: float64"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 800x600 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":100},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"*The strongest positive correlations with heart disease are chest pain type (0.432) and maximum heart rate (0.420), while the strongest negative correlations are the number of major vessels (−0.464), exercise induced angina (−0.436) and oldpeak (−0.429). Among the clinical measurements, oldpeak (−0.429) and maximum heart rate (0.420) are the strongest, while cholesterol (−0.081) and fasting blood sugar (−0.027) have almost no relationship with heart disease.*","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**3.\tPerform a logistic regression analysis to predict the presence of heart disease using all available features.**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Logistic regression using all features\n\nX = data_clean.drop(\"target\", axis=1)\ny = dat